(window.GROUP_QUIZZES=window.GROUP_QUIZZES||{})["pharmacology-i-exam-3-hf-inotropes-newer-agents-quiz-version-2"]={"title":"Other Heart Failure Drugs: Inotropes, Newer Agents & Aldosterone Antagonists Quiz 2 — Pharmacology I Exam 3","category":"Pharmacology I","exam":"Exam 3","sem":"fall-2026","questions":[{"q":"Which adverse effect of spironolactone in men may respond to a lower dose?","choices":["Hearing loss","Gynecomastia","Yellow-green halos","Dry cough"],"answer":1,"exp":"Correct. Gynecomastia occurs in a notable share of men on spironolactone and may respond to a lower dose; eplerenone rarely causes it. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 73"},{"q":"Which drug must not be taken together with sacubitril-valsartan?","choices":["Carvedilol","Lisinopril","Furosemide","Digoxin"],"answer":1,"exp":"Correct. An angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitor is not used with sacubitril-valsartan, and a washout period separates them. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 81"},{"q":"What is sacubitril-valsartan used to reduce in heart failure?","choices":["Cardiovascular death and hospitalization","Blood glucose and glycated hemoglobin","Intraocular pressure","Serum potassium"],"answer":0,"exp":"Correct. It is used to reduce the risk of cardiovascular death and hospitalization in patients with heart failure. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 81"},{"q":"Which channel does ivabradine block?","choices":["Hyperpolarization-activated channel","Voltage-gated calcium channel","Epithelial sodium channel","Delayed rectifier potassium channel"],"answer":0,"exp":"Correct. Ivabradine blocks the hyperpolarization-activated cyclic nucleotide-gated channel, inhibiting the pacemaker current. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 79"},{"q":"Which effects result from neprilysin inhibition?","choices":["Vasoconstriction, sodium retention and antidiuresis","Vasodilation, sodium retention and antidiuresis","Vasodilation, natriuresis and diuresis","Vasoconstriction, natriuresis and diuresis"],"answer":2,"exp":"Correct. Higher levels of natriuretic peptide and bradykinin cause vasodilation, natriuresis and diuresis. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 81"},{"q":"Which drug is sacubitril formulated with?","choices":["Valsartan","Lisinopril","Spironolactone","Metoprolol"],"answer":0,"exp":"Correct. Sacubitril is combined with valsartan, an angiotensin receptor blocker, in one product. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 81"},{"q":"Which pair of actions describes milrinone and inamrinone?","choices":["Inotropic and vasoconstrictor","Negative inotropic and vasodilator","Inotropic and diuretic","Inotropic and vasodilator"],"answer":3,"exp":"Correct. They directly stimulate myocardial contraction and also dilate arteries and veins in a balanced way. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 75"},{"q":"A patient in acute decompensated failure has high blood pressure and poor output. Which drug adds contractility and lowers afterload by dilating both arteries and veins?","choices":["Dobutamine","Digoxin","Ivabradine","Milrinone"],"answer":3,"exp":"Correct. Milrinone stimulates contraction directly and dilates arteries and veins, lowering afterload while raising output. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 75"},{"q":"Which heart failure patient is a candidate for ivabradine?","choices":["Atrial fibrillation with a rapid ventricular rate","Heart block with a very slow heart rate","Acute decompensation needing inotropic support","Sinus rhythm and rate above 70 on beta blockers"],"answer":3,"exp":"Correct. Ivabradine is for patients maxed out on beta blockers who remain in normal sinus rhythm with a heart rate above 70. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 79"},{"q":"For which use are milrinone and inamrinone approved?","choices":["Short-term use in acute decompensated failure","Long-term maintenance in stable failure","Prevention of failure in healthy adults","Outpatient rate control in atrial fibrillation"],"answer":0,"exp":"Correct. They are approved for short-term intravenous use in acute decompensated heart failure and then withdrawn once the patient stabilizes. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 76"},{"q":"What do sodium-glucose cotransporter 2 (SGLT2) inhibitors reduce in chronic heart failure?","choices":["Mortality and hospitalizations","Heart rate and contractility","Serum potassium and magnesium","Preload only"],"answer":0,"exp":"Correct. In stable, chronic reduced ejection fraction heart failure, they reduce mortality and hospitalizations. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 82"},{"q":"Which pair of adverse effects is common with sacubitril-valsartan?","choices":["Hypertension and hypokalemia","Hypotension and hyperkalemia","Gynecomastia and hirsutism","Phosphenes and bradycardia"],"answer":1,"exp":"Correct. Hypotension and hyperkalemia are among the most common effects, along with cough and renal insufficiency. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 81"},{"q":"Which messenger rises in heart muscle when phosphodiesterase 3 is inhibited?","choices":["Cyclic guanosine monophosphate","Inositol trisphosphate","Cyclic adenosine monophosphate","Nitric oxide in the myocardium"],"answer":2,"exp":"Correct. Blocking phosphodiesterase 3 prevents breakdown of cyclic adenosine monophosphate, which stimulates contraction. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 74"},{"q":"In which structure does ivabradine inhibit the pacemaker current?","choices":["Atrioventricular node","Sinoatrial node","Purkinje fibers","Ventricular myocardium"],"answer":1,"exp":"Correct. Ivabradine inhibits the pacemaker current in the sinoatrial node, lowering heart rate. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 79"},{"q":"For which condition were sodium-glucose cotransporter 2 (SGLT2) inhibitors originally developed?","choices":["Hypertension","Hyperlipidemia","Gout","Diabetes"],"answer":3,"exp":"Correct. They were originally developed for diabetes, since they cause the kidneys not to reabsorb glucose. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 82"},{"q":"A patient on ivabradine notices brief brightness in part of the visual field. What should the patient be told?","choices":["It is permanent retinal damage","It means digoxin toxicity","It requires stopping all heart failure drugs","It may resolve on its own"],"answer":3,"exp":"Correct. Visual phosphenes can resolve on their own, so the patient can be reassured and told to report persistent symptoms. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 80"},{"q":"Through which receptors does dopamine act?","choices":["Muscarinic and nicotinic receptors","Angiotensin and endothelin receptors","Dopamine and beta receptors","Imidazoline and alpha-2 receptors"],"answer":2,"exp":"Correct. Dopamine infusions act through dopamine and beta receptors. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 77"},{"q":"Which two drugs are sodium-glucose cotransporter 2 (SGLT2) inhibitors?","choices":["Sacubitril and valsartan","Milrinone and inamrinone","Dapagliflozin and empagliflozin","Spironolactone and eplerenone"],"answer":2,"exp":"Correct. Dapagliflozin and empagliflozin are the sodium-glucose cotransporter 2 (SGLT2) inhibitors listed for heart failure. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 82"},{"q":"Which counseling point applies to a patient starting a sodium-glucose cotransporter 2 (SGLT2) inhibitor?","choices":["Report urinary or genital fungal symptoms","Avoid all fluids","Add a potassium supplement","Stop the drug if urine contains glucose"],"answer":0,"exp":"Correct. Glucose in the urine encourages fungal growth, so symptoms of a urinary or genital fungal infection should be reported. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 82"},{"q":"Which phosphodiesterase 3 inhibitor causes less thrombocytopenia?","choices":["Inamrinone","Dobutamine","Milrinone","Dopamine"],"answer":2,"exp":"Correct. Thrombocytopenia occurs with both drugs, but milrinone causes less of it than inamrinone. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 76"},{"q":"Why do aldosterone antagonists slow progression of heart failure?","choices":["They raise preload through sodium retention","They slow left ventricular remodeling","They stimulate the sympathetic system","They block neprilysin"],"answer":1,"exp":"Correct. Neurohormonal inhibition of aldosterone slows remodeling of the left ventricle and so slows heart failure progression. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 73"},{"q":"Which receptor does dobutamine selectively stimulate?","choices":["Beta-2 adrenergic receptor","Beta-1 adrenergic receptor","Alpha-1 adrenergic receptor","Muscarinic receptor"],"answer":1,"exp":"Correct. Dobutamine is a selective beta-1 agonist, so it stimulates the force of contraction. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 77"}]};
